1
00:00:00,022 --> 00:00:01,817
Welcome to ResGrid Academy.

2
00:00:01,983 --> 00:00:06,124
In this lesson, we will match
subscription capacity to the roster.

3
00:00:06,308 --> 00:00:10,737
Large onboarding can stop at personnel
or unit limits when capacity has

4
00:00:10,738 --> 00:00:12,421
not been reviewed in advance.

5
00:00:12,590 --> 00:00:16,303
We will explain the features,
the setup decisions, and a

6
00:00:16,303 --> 00:00:18,417
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:19,206 --> 00:00:24,213
Before inviting forty new members, an
administrator confirms the plan has room

8
00:00:24,213 --> 00:00:26,683
or asks the managing member to change it.

9
00:00:26,872 --> 00:00:31,197
Adding members or units stops at the
plan limit, so check the remaining

10
00:00:31,198 --> 00:00:33,048
room before a large onboarding.

11
00:00:33,239 --> 00:00:37,210
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

12
00:00:37,210 --> 00:00:39,650
scenarios, not default settings.

13
00:00:40,473 --> 00:00:44,500
Base plans and capacity, your
plan, its personnel and unit

14
00:00:44,501 --> 00:00:46,257
limits, and your add-ons.

15
00:00:46,477 --> 00:00:49,942
Check the remaining room before
adding many members or units.

16
00:00:50,772 --> 00:00:53,667
For the training scenario,
work in this order.

17
00:00:53,888 --> 00:00:59,287
Step one: review the observed base
plan, personnel count, and unit count.

18
00:00:59,522 --> 00:01:03,508
Step two: compare planned
onboarding with available capacity.

19
00:01:03,718 --> 00:01:07,112
Step three: review add-on
entitlements and their separate

20
00:01:07,120 --> 00:01:09,113
configuration prerequisites.

21
00:01:09,943 --> 00:01:11,569
Now verify the result.

22
00:01:11,794 --> 00:01:15,395
Check observed subscription evidence
and current resource counts.

23
00:01:15,585 --> 00:01:19,544
Use the owning billing screen for
any authorized subscription change.

24
00:01:19,741 --> 00:01:23,088
A common problem to watch
for, missing billing evidence

25
00:01:23,104 --> 00:01:24,905
means capacity is unknown.

26
00:01:25,108 --> 00:01:28,536
Only the managing member
performs subscription changes.

27
00:01:29,333 --> 00:01:31,163
Your practice task is simple.

28
00:01:31,357 --> 00:01:34,863
Compare current counts with
the proposed roster expansion.

29
00:01:35,062 --> 00:01:38,991
Document headroom and optional
add-ons without purchasing anything.

30
00:01:39,184 --> 00:01:43,704
Record the result, who owns the
follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

31
00:01:43,839 --> 00:01:47,764
Use the linked feature scripts for
the detailed screen recording plan.
